        "name": "The Status Speaks Twice Rule",
        "body": "A status colour never appears alone. Pair it with a word (\"Failed\", \"Protected\") or an icon, so the meaning survives 1-Bit, colour blindness and screen readers.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Unknown Is Not Green Rule",
        "body": "Green means verified protected. Loading, unknown or unavailable states use neutral ink and say what's unknown. Never default to a success colour or a zero.",
